  id: Bladder
  partName: Bladder
  descriptionChunks:
  - The urinary bladder is a hollow, muscular organ responsible for storing urine
    before excretion. It expands as it fills and contracts during urination to expel
    waste through the urethra. This organ plays a crucial role in maintaining fluid
    balance and removing metabolic waste products from the bloodstream.
  - Its proper functioning ensures controlled elimination and prevents accumulation
    of toxins, supporting overall homeostasis and efficient functioning of the urinary
    system.
